#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0253.1 expect=violation domain=RELREC
#note "THE SECOND-CONJUNCT PIN (Fix #295 / M3-D16). ONE row whose only difference from row 3 of -invalid-RELREC (deliberately silent) is the RELTYPE cell: BOTH is not a member of the sheet's enumeration. The sheet Rule cell is a conjunction -- 'USUBJID, POOLID, and IDVARVAL are null AND (RELTYPE = \"ONE\" OR RELTYPE = \"MANY\")' -- and only the first half was implemented, so an out-of-enumeration RELTYPE went unreported. The added `RELTYPE not in [\"ONE\", \"MANY\"]` disjunct is the shape CDISC-SEND-0253, -0201, -0255 and -0390 already ship; the pair with row 3 is exactly discriminating."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 RELTYPE=BOTH
dataset RELREC label="Related Records"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col POOLID   type=Char label="Pool Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col RELTYPE  type=Char label="Relationship Type"
col RELID    type=Char label="Relationship Identifier"
---
S1 | MA |  |  | MASEQ |  | BOTH | R1
---
